      "takeaway": "This survey reviews Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models for robotics as a full-stack integration of software and hardware, rather than focusing narrowly on action representations or high-level architectures. It organizes the literature around strategy and architectural transition, architectures and building blocks, modality-specific processing techniques, and learning paradigms, then extends to robot platforms, data collection strategies, publicly available datasets, data augmentation methods, and evaluation benchmarks for real-world deployment. The authors frame the goal as practical guidance for applying VLAs to real-world robotic systems, and they provide a project website with references categorized by training approach, evaluation method, modality, and dataset. Read it as a knowledge map for locating work across the VLA stack and for tracing how data, evaluation, and platforms connect to deployment.",
